{{Codex|This devastating automatic crossbow is the perfect marriage of ancient Earth weaponry and Tenno technology.}}
The '''Zhuge''' is a Tenno automatic crossbow. It boasts impressive damage that is complemented by its very high [[status chance]], limited by its projectile nature and very slow fire rate.

This weapon can be sold for ‍{{cc|7,500}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*On kill, bodies will follow the bolt that killed them, damaging anyone in their path and pinning the corpse to walls.
*Can use the bow-exclusive {{M|Thunderbolt}} mod.
*Counts as a bow in regards to [[fire rate]] mods, doubling the fire rate bonus.
*Innate {{Pol|Madurai}} polarity.

{{Advantages|class=Crossbow|
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Crossbow|
}}

{{Advantages|class=Rifle|
*Tied with {{Weapon|Panthera}}/{{Weapon|Panthera Prime}} for the highest base damage of all fully automatic weapons.
*High base [[accuracy]].
*[[Silent]].
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Rifle|
*Projectiles have travel time.
*Third lowest [[fire rate]] of all fully automatic weapons, after {{Weapon|Attica}}/{{Weapon|Panthera Prime}} and {{Weapon|Panthera}}.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Zhuge Prime}}

*Bolts do not explode on impact by default; thus no [[Stagger|self-stagger]] effect.

==Acquisition==
The Zhuge's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*Can be used on bow-only [[Sortie]] missions.

==Tips==
*While possessing an Auto trigger, the Zhuge is best used when fired in bursts to better aim shots and manage its small magazine. On the other hand, its automatic fire combined with its native knockback makes it good when strafing against multiple enemies, or shooting a single tough enemy multiple times.
*{{M|Thunderbolt}} synergizes well with the Zhuge due to the weapon's magazine size and automatic trigger, giving it a very high chance of triggering explosions within a shorter amount of time than conventional bows. This makes the Zhuge more proficient at crowd-control than single-shot bows like the {{Weapon|Dread}}, with its full-auto fire allowing one to strafe an area with explosive bolts to deal damage against multiple enemies. With {{M|Cautious Shot}} it will still stagger you if caught in the explosion radius.

==Trivia==
*The Zhuge was originally introduced in [[WARFRAME (China)|Warframe China]] as a timed-exclusive item, alongside the {{Weapon|Ninkondi}} and {{Weapon|Spira}}.
*The Zhuge is named after the Chinese word for the [[wikipedia:Repeating crossbow|repeating crossbow]], ''Zhūgé nǔ'' (諸葛弩), literally meaning "the Zhuge [Liang] crossbow", in turn named after its purported inventor [[wikipedia:Zhuge Liang|Zhuge Liang]]. Zhuge Liang was a Chinese chancellor that lived during the Three Kingdoms Period of China, and is considered one of the greatest strategists of the era.
*The Zhuge is the fourth crossbow introduced in the game, after the {{Weapon|Attica}} and {{Weapon|Ballistica}}/{{Weapon|Rakta Ballistica}}.

