{{WeaponInfoboxAutomatic}}
{{Codex|Hammer the enemy with this light-bodied heavy hitter. Featuring a double-action trigger that fires hard and fast.}}
The '''Zylok''' is a duplex-fire, cut-down variant of the {{Weapon|Sybaris}}, boasting high {{D|Slash}} damage and [[status chance]] at the cost of [[critical chance]] and fire rate. The weapon can fire one bullet at a time by first holding down the fire button, then releasing, allowing more precision shots and ammo conservation.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Slash}} damage.
*Can equip the Zylok-exclusive {{M|Eximus Advantage}} mod.
*Unique trigger type allows for two rapid shots against tough targets, or careful shot management against many weaker opponents. First shot on button press, the second on button release.

{{Advantages|
*Good [[accuracy]].
}}

{{Disadvantages|}}

{{WeaponComparison|Zylok Prime}}

==Acquisition==
The Zylok is potentially sold by [[Baro Ki'Teer]] in the Concourse section of the [[Tenno]] [[Relay]] for {{cc|200,000}} and {{dc|500}}. Note that Baro Ki'Teer's stock changes with each appearance, and this weapon may not be available on a succeeding appearance.

The weapon can be [[Trade System|traded]], but only for unranked copies without [[Forma]] and [[Orokin Catalyst]] installed. The trading recipient must also have a [[Mastery Rank]] of at least 6.

===History===
This weapon was introduced during the [[The Pyrus Project]] [[event]]. To receive the weapon, players had to complete all four tasks related to the reconstruction of the Strata [[Relay]]: contributing '''30''' {{Resource|Pyrus Essence}} and '''5''' [[The Pyrus Project#Contribute Relay Strut Components|Relay Strut Components]], completing '''1''' [[Simaris]] [[Synthesis#Daily Synthesis Task|Daily Synthesis Task]], and defeating [[the Grustrag Three]] '''3''' times. The weapon came with a free weapon slot and a pre-installed [[Orokin Catalyst]].

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Zylok Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Zylok Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Trivia==
*The Zylok is the first and so far only duplex-fire weapon outside of the {{Weapon|Tigris}} family of shotguns.
*While technically duplex in nature, it does make it the third 2-shot burst fire pistol in the game, alongside the {{Weapon|Akjagara}} and {{Weapon|Kraken}}.
*The Zylok appears to have a rotating turret magazine, as seen in the {{Weapon|Sybaris}}, which is modeled after the [https://www.historynet.com/the-porter-turret-rifle-ingenious-features-yet-inherently-flawed/ Porter Turret Rifle]. The experimental design was percussion-cap and had a cylinder with radial, outward facing chambers. This was quickly deemed too dangerous, since at least one chamber pointed towards the user's face, and it was possible to accidentally "chainfire" or fire all shots at once. 

